let's get to the political bombshell  that exploded today after the  publication of an interview with  Christine Blasi Ford who up until now  had anonymously claimed that Brett  Kavanaugh tried to physically force  himself on her while drunk at a high  school party nearly four decades ago  when he was 17 years old the interview  includes new details and corroboration  in the form of therapist's notes from  six years ago I want to make sure you're  fully informed with all the facts you  need so here's the timeline in July  Christine Blasi Ford wrote to her member  of Congress California Democrat Anna  Eshoo detailing the assault and asking  to remain anonymous congresswoman Eshoo  then forwarded the letter to Senator  Dianne Feinstein the ranking member of  the Senate Judiciary Committee which of  course was handling the Cavanaugh  confirmation  Dianne Feinstein shared the contents of  the letter with a small number of aides  and fellow senators but honored the  request for anonymity neither the  existence of the letter or its contents  were brought up at any stage of the  confirmation process either publicly or  privately on Wednesday last week online  news outlet the intercept published a  story about the letter accusing senator  Feinstein of withholding it the next day  Feinstein still trying to honor the  request for anonymity referred the  matter to the FBI and made that referral  public without revealing its contents  that set off a media firestorm which  resulted in Ronan Farrow from The New  Yorker going public with the allegations  still at that point anonymous ones Brett  Kavanaugh has categorically and  unequivocally denied this allegation and  the Judiciary Committee vote on his  nomination remains scheduled for this  Thursday the letter itself has now been  published Democrats are united in  calling for a delay while this matter is  fully investigated some Republicans  including Lindsey Graham and Jeff Flake  say they want to hear directly from Miss  Ford the alleged victim before moving  forward and now Senator Chuck Grassley  chairman of the Judiciary Committee says  he is actively working on following up  with  both Brett Kavanaugh and Miss Ford  before proceeding with the confirmation  process now those are the facts and  based on what we know now at this point  here's my opinion one none of this  changes the fact that Brett Kavanaugh is  qualified for a seat on the court and  that his judicial philosophy is not only  in line with what Donald Trump promised  in the 26 campaign 2016 campaign but  good for the country too Dianne  Feinstein has been unfairly castigated  in all this it was not her but the  intercept that put this matter in the  public domain three some on the Left  have politicized this in a deeply  disturbing way just look at this  statement from the liberal pro-choice  group narrow quote the charge of sexual  assault against Brett Kavanaugh is  disqualifying and we call on him to  immediately withdraw his nomination for  the Supreme Court the charge an  accusation on its own is disqualifying  imagine if we accepted that as the new  standard anyone could make up anything  about a candidate or nominee that they  oppose politically destroy them  personally and prevent them from public  office our republic depends on good men  and women who love their country and  love their community stepping into the  arena to serve and lead their fellow  citizens this outrageous new standard  that any attack at all any allegation  can end someone's career that is the  true threat to democracy not president  Trump as all these leftists claim this  is quite simply the rule of the mob and  we must not allow it to prevail
 

